basisOfSymmetricCurves -- produces a basis of symmetric curves
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        basisOfSymmetricCurves(8)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * B, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

This function returns the list of *note F curves: F curve, $\{F_{1,1,i,n-i-2}:
1 \leq i \leq [n/2]\}$.  This set of curves is a basis for
$H_2(\bar{M}_{0,n})_{Q}^{S_n}$; see e.g. *note [AGSS]: Bibliography,.  The
symmetric F-curve $F_{1,1,i,n-i-2}$ is represented by the list of integers
\{1,1,i,n-i-2\}.



+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : basisOfSymmetricCurves(8)                 |
|                                               |
|o1 = {{5, 1, 1, 1}, {4, 2, 1, 1}, {3, 3, 1, 1}}|
|                                               |
|o1 : List                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------+

Ways to use basisOfSymmetricCurves:
===================================

  * "basisOfSymmetricCurves(ZZ)"

