conformalBlockRank -- computes the rank of the conformal block vector bundle
****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        conformalBlockRank(V)
  * Inputs:
      * V, an instance of the type *note ConformalBlockVectorBundle:
        ConformalBlockVectorBundle,,
  * Outputs:
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

This function uses propagation and factorization to recursively compute ranks
in terms of the ranks on $\bar{M}_{0,3}$.  These are determined by the
so-called fusion rules and are computed via the function *note
fusionCoefficient: (LieAlgebraRepresentations)fusionCoefficient, in the *note
LieAlgebraRepresentations: (LieAlgebraRepresentations)Top, package.  See *note
[Beauville]: Bibliography, for details on these topics.



In the example below we compute the rank of the conformal block bundle
$V(sl_3,2,(\omega_1,\omega_1,\omega_2,\omega_2))$.



+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : sl_3=simpleLieAlgebra("A",2);                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : V=conformalBlockVectorBundle(sl_3,2,{{1,0},{1,0},{0,1},{0,1}},0)|
|                                                                     |
|o2 = V                                                               |
|                                                                     |
|o2 : Conformal block vector bundle on M-0-4-bar                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : conformalBlockRank(V)                                           |
|                                                                     |
|o3 = 2                                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use conformalBlockRank:
===============================

  * "conformalBlockRank(ConformalBlockVectorBundle)"

