psiDivisorM0nbar -- returns the class of the divisor $\Psi$
***********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        psiDivisorM0nbar(14)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * D, an instance of the type *note SymmetricDivisorM0nbar:
        SymmetricDivisorM0nbar,,

Description
===========

Let $U$ be the universal family over $M=\bar{M}_{0,n}$, let $\omega_{U/M}$ be
the relative dualizing sheaf, and let $\sigma_i: M \rightarrow U$ be the
sections defining the marked points. The divisors $\psi_i$ are defined by
$\psi_i := \sigma_i^*(\omega_{U/M})$.  We define the class $\Psi$ by $\Psi =
\psi_1 + ... + \psi_n.$



