SymmetricDivisorM0nbar -- the class of S_n symmetric divisors on the moduli space of stable n-pointed genus 0 curves
********************************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

This type implements $S_n$ symmetric divisors on the moduli space of stable
n-pointed genus 0 curves $\bar{M}_{0,n}$.



The *note standard basis: standard basis, of the $Q$-vector space of $S_n$
symmetric divisors on $\bar{M}_{0,n}$ is given by the boundary divisors B_i, as
we now explain.   Let $\Delta_I$ be the closure of the locus of curves with two
irreducible components meeting at one node such that the marked points with
labels in $I$ lie on the first component, and the marked points with labels in
$I^c$ lie on the second component.  Then $B_i= \sum_{\#I=i} \Delta_I$, and the
divisors $B_2, ..., B_{[n/2]}$ form a basis of the space of symmetric divisors.
See *note [KM]: Bibliography,.



Symmetric divisors are implemented as hash tables.  The key "NumberOfPoints"
records the number of marked points, i.e., the $n$ in $\bar{M}_{0,n}$.  The
keys must be integers between 2 and $[n/2]$; the value of the key i is the
coefficient of $B_i$ when a divisor $D$ is written in the standard basis.



An object of the "SymmetricDivisorM0nbar" class can be created using the
function *note symmetricDivisorM0nbar: symmetricDivisorM0nbar, in either one of
two ways: by entering $n$ and a linear polynomial in the $B_i$'s, or entering
$n$ and a list of coefficients.



Methods are included for adding two symmetric divisors, negating a divisor,
multiplying a divisor by a scalar, and testing equality of two divisors.  The
function *note coefficientList: coefficientList, returns the list of the
coefficients.

Functions and methods returning an object of class SymmetricDivisorM0nbar:
==========================================================================

  * *note canonicalDivisorM0nbar: canonicalDivisorM0nbar, -- returns the class
    of the canonical divisor on the moduli space of stable n-pointed genus 0
    curves
  * *note kappaDivisorM0nbar: kappaDivisorM0nbar, -- the class of the divisor
    kappa
  * *note psiDivisorM0nbar: psiDivisorM0nbar, -- returns the class of the
    divisor $\Psi$
  * *note scale: scale, -- reduces a list or divisor by the gcd of its
    coefficients
  * *note symmetricDivisorM0nbar: symmetricDivisorM0nbar, -- create a symmetric
    divisor on the moduli space of stable pointed genus 0 curves
  * *note symmetrizedConformalBlockDivisor: symmetrizedConformalBlockDivisor,
    -- computes the symmetrization of the first Chern class of a conformal
    block vector bundle

