SymmetricDivisorM0nbar + SymmetricDivisorM0nbar -- add two $S_n$ symmetric divisors
***********************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note +: (Macaulay2Doc)+,
  * Usage: 
        D+E
  * Inputs:
      * D, an instance of the type *note SymmetricDivisorM0nbar:
        SymmetricDivisorM0nbar,,
      * E, an instance of the type *note SymmetricDivisorM0nbar:
        SymmetricDivisorM0nbar,,
  * Outputs:
      * F, an instance of the type *note SymmetricDivisorM0nbar:
        SymmetricDivisorM0nbar,,

Description
===========

Let $Pic(\bar{M}_{0,n})_Q^{S_n}$ denote the vector space of $S_n$-invariant
divisors with rational coefficients.  Here, given two $S_n$ symmetric
$Q$-divisors $D$ and $E$ on $\bar{M}_{0,n}$, the function returns $D+E$.



+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D=symmetricDivisorM0nbar(6,{1/2,1/3})  |
|                                            |
|     1      1                               |
|o1 = -*B  + -*B                             |
|     2  2   3  3                            |
|                                            |
|o1 : S_6-symmetric divisor on M-0-6-bar     |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : E=symmetricDivisorM0nbar(6,2*B_2+3*B_3)|
|                                            |
|o2 = 2*B  + 3*B                             |
|        2      3                            |
|                                            |
|o2 : S_6-symmetric divisor on M-0-6-bar     |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : D+E                                    |
|                                            |
|     5      10                              |
|o3 = -*B  + --*B                            |
|     2  2    3  3                           |
|                                            |
|o3 : S_6-symmetric divisor on M-0-6-bar     |
+--------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note SymmetricDivisorM0nbar + SymmetricDivisorM0nbar:
    SymmetricDivisorM0nbar + SymmetricDivisorM0nbar, -- add two $S_n$ symmetric
    divisors
