SymmetricDivisorM0nbar == SymmetricDivisorM0nbar -- test equality of two symmetric divisor classes on $\bar{M}_{0,n}$
*********************************************************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ==: (Macaulay2Doc)==,
  * Usage: 
        D==E
  * Inputs:
      * D, an instance of the type *note SymmetricDivisorM0nbar:
        SymmetricDivisorM0nbar,,
      * E, an instance of the type *note SymmetricDivisorM0nbar:
        SymmetricDivisorM0nbar,,
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Two objects of type SymmetricDivisorM0nbar are equal if their underlying hash
tables have the same pairs.



+------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D=symmetricDivisorM0nbar(6,{2,1})                |
|                                                      |
|o1 = 2*B  + B                                         |
|        2    3                                        |
|                                                      |
|o1 : S_6-symmetric divisor on M-0-6-bar               |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : E=scale symmetricDivisorM0nbar(6,288*B_2+144*B_3)|
|                                                      |
|o2 = 2*B  + B                                         |
|        2    3                                        |
|                                                      |
|o2 : S_6-symmetric divisor on M-0-6-bar               |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : D==E                                             |
|                                                      |
|o3 = true                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note SymmetricDivisorM0nbar == SymmetricDivisorM0nbar:
    SymmetricDivisorM0nbar == SymmetricDivisorM0nbar, -- test equality of two
    symmetric divisor classes on $\bar{M}_{0,n}$
